    "biography": {
      "concept": "The Balcones fault line, a landform with feelings (Act 3)",
      "notes": "Since the Shattering the Balcones fault has had limited agency and a lot of feelings. It does not shake; it slides. Horizons shear sideways, roads drift out of agreement with themselves, fence lines kink, and creeks insist they were always somewhere else. It is not an enemy. It is tired of being ignored. Travellers get past it by soothing it with incense and ceremony (it sneezes), telling it a story, striking a deal, or building a bridge. It does not speak, but people who've learned to read its trace say it writes in lists."
    }
  },
